ere--since I'm not treating Λ9 in Iβ1--or in","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"candidate_unverified"},{"bbox":[300,1281,2250,1322],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf414-native-0016","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf414-note-unresolved-1","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":16,"source":"human_draft","structure_status":"candidate_unverified","text":"an appendix}. but both Jaeger and Ross immediately infer from this that Aristotle wrote this passage at Assos, i.e. in","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"candidate_unverified"},{"bbox":[300,1329,2223,1370],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf414-native-0017","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf414-note-unresolved-1","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":17,"source":"human_draft","structure_status":"candidate_unverified","text":"the period shortly after Plato’s death, which does not follow in the slightest--Aristotle would always have regarded","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"candidate_unverified"},{"bbox":[300,1376,2248,1418],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf414-native-0018","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf414-note-unresolved-1","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":18,"source":"human_draft","structure_status":"candidate_unverified","text":"himself as a better Platonist than Speusippus, and there are no passages anywhere where he rejects a good-itself (see","transcription_status"